From 6a6725b267d4283b9e7e2c27638f1cae0b2e2009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ultras <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:44:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] mt7981: WR3000H, PHY reset, GPT timers, built-in PHY,
 thermal

- cudy-wr3000h machine (2.5G WAN RTL8221B, PHY reset on the MDIO bus).
- WAN PHY hardware reset on GPIO3: while held in reset the PHY does not
  answer on MDIO, released with power-on register values.
- pinctrl exports pad levels to board devices.
- RTL8221B: SerDes command bit (VEND1 0x7587 bit0) self-clears (OpenWrt
  25.12 waits for it; WAN had no carrier).
- APXGPT general purpose timers (stock Cudy BL2 delays use them).
- MT7981 built-in GbE PHY at MDIO 0 with analog calibration handshake
  and eFuse calibration data.
- Thermal sensor: eFuse calibration and a live TEMP_MSR0 (~45 C).
- pcap: optional functions, skipped under Wine.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
